  "Delinea announced its acquisition of StrongDM on January 15, 2026 and completed it on March 5, 2026; whether the factory methodology continues under new ownership is unverifiable.": 1,
  "Reported cautions: building the DTU required significant engineering effort, fit beyond integration-heavy domains is unclear, teams must accept not reading generated code, and the approach is less battle-tested than human-reviewed workflows.": 1,
  "Ry Walker's analysis calls scenario holdouts a design claim that validation stored outside the codebase is less vulnerable to reward hacking, not proven prevention.": 1,
  "Scenario holdouts are a design claim that scenarios stored outside the codebase are less vulnerable to reward hacking; this is not proven prevention of it.": 1,
  "StrongDM open-sourced Attractor, a non-interactive coding agent structured as a graph of phases, as a natural-language spec rather than an implementation (Apache-2.0, ~1.3K GitHub stars as of September 23, 2026), and also open-sourced CXDB, a context store for agents.": 1,
  "StrongDM's charter states two rules: 'Code must not be written by humans' and 'Code must not be reviewed by humans'; code is treated as opaque weights whose correctness is inferred from behavior, not inspection.": 1,
  "StrongDM's operating heuristic is that if a team has not spent at least $1,000 on tokens today per human engineer, the factory has room for improvement; this is a spend heuristic, not a measured productivity result.": 1,
  "The Digital Twin Universe clones Okta, Jira, Slack, Google Docs, Google Drive, and Google Sheets.": 1,
  "The Factory became viable after Claude 3.5's October 2024 revision enabled 'compounding correctness' in long-horizon agentic workflows, whereas earlier models accumulated errors until the product 'collapsed'.": 1,
  "The factory essay reached the Hacker News front page in February 2026 (304 points, 459 comments); validation ideas (DTU, holdouts) drew admiration while the 'no human review' charter for a security product drew the harshest criticism.": 1,
  "The initial foundation of the Factory was Cursor YOLO mode, and the validation loop uses an LLM-as-judge to evaluate satisfaction.": 1
